H2619.def:
A man of the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1 Chroniques 3:20; 
son of: Zerubbabel (H2216); 
brother of: Meshullam (H4918H), Hananiah (H2608L), Shelomith (H8019I), Hashubah (H2807), Ohel (H0169), Berechiah (H1296), Jushab-hesed (H3142), Abiud (G0010) 
§ Hasadiah = "Jehovah has been faithful"
a son of Zerubbabel

H2641.def:
A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 2 Rois 22:14; 
father of: Tikvah (H8616); also called Hasrah at 2 Chroniques 34:22;
Another name of char.chas (חַרְחַס "Harhas" H2745) 
§ Hasrah = "lack"
grandfather of Shallum who was the husband of Huldah, the prophetess; also spelled 'Harhas'

H2650G.def:
A man of the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at 1 Chroniques 7:12; 
son of: Ir (H5893); 
brother of: Shuppim (H8206) and Maacah (H4601M)
§ Huppim = "protected"
the head of a Benjamite family

H2650H.def:
A man of the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Genèse 46:21; 
son of: Benjamin (H1144); 
brother of: Bela (H1106A), Becher (H1071), Ashbel (H0788), Gera (H1617), Naaman (H5283), Ehi (H0278), Rosh (H7220), Muppim (H4649), Ard (H0714), Ahiram (H0297) and Jediael (H3043); also called Huphamite at Nombres 26:39; Hupham at Nombres 26:39; Huram in1Ch.8.5; 
§ Huppim = "protected"
the head of a Benjamite family

H2652.def:
A man living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1 Samuel 1:3; 
son of: Eli (H5941); 
brother of: Phinehas (H6372H) 
§ Hophni = "pugilist"
one of the two sons of Eli who were priests at Shiloh and were noted for their brutality and lust; their sinfulness provoked a curse against their father's house and were judged by the Lord when they took the ark into battle; the ark was lost and both brothers were killed and Eli died when he heard the news

H2660A.def:
A man of the tribe of Manasseh living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Nombres 26:32; 
son of: Gilead (H1568H); 
brother of: Abiezer (H0044I), Helek (H2507), Asriel (H0844), Shechem (H7928) and Shemida (H8061); 
father of: Zelophehad (H6765)
Also named: cheph.ri (חֶפְרִי "Hepherite" H2662)
§ Hepher = "a well"
1) youngest son of Gilead and head of the family of Hepherites
2) son of Asher, the father of Tekoa
3) the Mecherathite, one of David's mighty warriors

H2660G.def:
A man of the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1 Chroniques 4:6; 
son of: Ashhur (H0806) and Naarah (H5292B); 
brother of: Ahuzzam (H0275), Temeni (H8488) and Haahashtari (H0326); 
half-brother of: Zereth (H6889), Izhar (H3328), Ethnan (H0869) and Koz (H6976)
§ Hepher = "a well"
1) a place in ancient Canaan, west of the Jordan, conquered by Joshua 
2) a place in Judah, probably the same as 1 above

H2662.def:
Someone descended from Hepher who was a man of the tribe of Manasseh living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Nombres 26:32; 
son of: Gilead (H1568H); 
brother of: Abiezer (H0044I), Helek (H2507), Asriel (H0844), Shechem (H7928) and Shemida (H8061); 
father of: Zelophehad (H6765)
Group of che.pher (חֵ֫פֶר "Hepher" H2660A) 
§ Hepherites , of Hepher "a pit" or "shame"
descendants of Hepher, son of Gilead

H2688.def:
Hazezon-tamar = "dividing the date-palm"
a town situated in the desert Judah;
Another name of en ge.di (עֵין גֶּ֫דִי "Engedi" H5872)

H2695.def:
A man living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 2 Samuel 23:35; also called in KJV: Hezrai; 
§ Hezro or Hezrai = "enclosed"
the Carmelite, one of David's 30 mighty warriors in his guard

H2696H.def:
A man of the tribe of Judah living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Genèse 46:12; 
son of: Perez (H6557); 
brother of: Hamul (H2538); married to daughter_of_Machir (H4353I) and Abiah (H0029J); 
father of: Ram (H7410), Jerahmeel (H3396), Caleb (H3612H), Segub (H7687H) and Ashhur (H0806)
§ Hezron = "surrounded by a wall"
1) a son of Reuben
2) a son of Pharez and grandson of Judah
3) a place in the extreme south of Judah

H2697.def:
Someone descended from Hezron who was a man of the tribe of Judah living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Genèse 46:12; 
son of: Perez (H6557); 
brother of: Hamul (H2538); married to daughter_of_Machir (H4353I) and Abiah (H0029J); 
father of: Ram (H7410), Jerahmeel (H3396), Caleb (H3612H), Segub (H7687H) and Ashhur (H0806)
Group of chets.ron (חֶצְרוֹן "Hezron" H2696H) 
§ Hezronites , of Hezron "enclosed" or "division of song"
a descendant of Hezron
